<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Weights importances in experiments initialization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have tested the influence on the importance of random and magnitude-based weights for tested base models in both tested compression methods. The magnitude-based method produced the worst performance than random pruning for each computation method <a href="#A1.T3" title="In A.2 All experiments ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Projected Compression: Trainable Projection for Efficient Transformer Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
